WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.070 --> 00:00:07.340
Discovery Channel's Deadliest Catch depicts
the real-life risks of Alaskan crab fishing.

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:10.280
However, the show doesn't quite catch everything.

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:14.780
Let's dock the Sea Star, Time Bandit, and
all other boats to get a closer look at Deadliest

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:16.209
Catch.

00:00:16.209 --> 00:00:17.830
ELLIOTT NEESE'S REHAB STAY

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:22.090
During season 11 of Deadliest Catch, then
Captain Elliott Neese abruptly handed over

00:00:22.090 --> 00:00:26.589
the helm of the Saga to first mate Jeff Folk
and left his ship—leaving viewers wondering

00:00:26.589 --> 00:00:28.539
why he went AWOL.

00:00:28.539 --> 00:00:32.300
After rumors swirled in tabloids about his
addiction problems, Neese himself tweeted

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:37.850
in May 2015 that he'd entered a 60-day program
at Passages Malibu for an undisclosed program.

00:00:37.850 --> 00:00:41.840
He wrote that he'd "had issues," but after
his stay at Passages, had "a new outlook on

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:43.910
things now."

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:45.410
NEESE'S RESTRAINING ORDER

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:47.940
It seems Elliott Neese is a magnet for trouble.

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:51.860
Back in 2012, he got himself slapped with
a restraining order, according to documents

00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:53.520
cited by Entertainment Weekly.

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:57.760
It seems he'd been harassing his baby mamma
Valerie Gunderson for the better part of a

00:00:57.760 --> 00:00:58.780
month, maybe more.

00:00:58.780 --> 00:01:02.870
In her petition, Gunderson said she feared
for her personal safety "in the event that

00:01:02.870 --> 00:01:04.750
Elliott ‘snaps’ so to speak."

00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:08.750
She also claimed that during one incident
in 2010, Neese got so angry that he destroyed

00:01:08.750 --> 00:01:13.090
her television—and then started burning
her clothes in the fireplace.

00:01:13.090 --> 00:01:17.490
It seems that for Gunderson, snagging Neese's
heart was a pretty deadly catch in and of

00:01:17.490 --> 00:01:18.490
itself.

00:01:18.490 --> 00:01:19.900
FREDDY MAUGATAI: BATHROOM BRAWLER

00:01:19.900 --> 00:01:25.240
Apparently, Feleti "Freddy" Maugatai has some
mixed-martial arts ambitions.

00:01:25.240 --> 00:01:29.210
According to a criminal complaint obtained
by TMZ, Maugatai got involved in a fight against

00:01:29.210 --> 00:01:33.040
a husband and wife team in the bathroom of
the Grand Aleutian Hotel back in December

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:34.040
2011.

00:01:34.040 --> 00:01:37.770
Maugatai claims he was defending himself when
he put the husband in a headlock and shoved

00:01:37.770 --> 00:01:39.270
the guy's wife.

00:01:39.270 --> 00:01:40.990
Police arrested him, despite his story.

00:01:40.990 --> 00:01:45.020
He was later fired from his ship for an unrelated
incident, but maybe he should look into bringing

00:01:45.020 --> 00:01:47.149
his untapped fighting prowess to the octagon.

00:01:47.149 --> 00:01:50.259
Each of his fights could be called "Deadliest
Match!"

00:01:50.259 --> 00:01:52.290
Don't deny it: you'd watch it.

00:01:52.290 --> 00:01:54.170
JAKE HARRIS: DRUNK DRIVER

00:01:54.170 --> 00:01:58.040
Jake Harris, son of the late Captain Phil
Harris, seems to have made a smooth transition

00:01:58.040 --> 00:02:00.439
from crab fisherman to reality star.

00:02:00.439 --> 00:02:04.289
Back in 2010, Jake was arrested for a hit
and run, driving under the influence, and

00:02:04.289 --> 00:02:09.000
driving with a suspended license after crashing
his BMW in Seattle, according to People Magazine.

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:12.160
Supposedly, Jake had a tough time dealing
with his father's death.

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:15.070
But while that may explain his actions, it
certainly didn't justify them.

00:02:15.070 --> 00:02:18.150
Plus, it's not the best way to honor his father's
legacy.

00:02:18.150 --> 00:02:20.770
Neither was his other indiscretion…

00:02:20.770 --> 00:02:22.920
JAKE HARRIS' DRUG STRUGGLES

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:28.140
In November 2010, TMZ reported that Captain
Derek Ray, of the Cornelia Marie, called police

00:02:28.140 --> 00:02:31.950
to the boat because he suspected Jake Harris
was abusing drugs while at sea.

00:02:31.950 --> 00:02:35.770
Police discovered "paraphernalia," but it
wasn't enough to charge Jake with any crime.

00:02:35.770 --> 00:02:40.890
A few years later, Jake was noticeably absent
from Deadliest Catch's 2013 promos.

00:02:40.890 --> 00:02:45.040
According to his brother Josh, via Huffington
Post, Jake was "lost in drugs," obviously

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:46.770
still reeling from his father's death.

00:02:46.770 --> 00:02:49.260
"Jake’s gotta take care of his own stuff
right now.

00:02:49.260 --> 00:02:51.480
Deal with his demons," said Josh.

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:56.510
Fortunately, as of August 2015, Jake was clean
and captaining his father's old boat.

00:02:56.510 --> 00:02:59.240
JOSHUA TEL WARNER: BANK ROBBER

00:02:59.240 --> 00:03:03.090
Despite the crimes committed by other Deadliest
Catchers, Joshua Tel Warner might be the biggest

00:03:03.090 --> 00:03:04.770
criminal of them all.

00:03:04.770 --> 00:03:08.360
According to CBS News, Warner was wanted for
a series of bank robberies that took place

00:03:08.360 --> 00:03:11.340
in Oregon from 2007 to 2009.

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:13.110
So what did Warner do to lay low?

00:03:13.110 --> 00:03:14.580
He appeared on television.

00:03:14.580 --> 00:03:18.670
Oregon law enforcement officials recognized
Warner during a 2010 episode of Deadliest

00:03:18.670 --> 00:03:21.590
Catch and immediately issued a warrant for
his arrest.

00:03:21.590 --> 00:03:25.810
Warner plead guilty to reduce his prison sentence
from 30 years to nine and a half years.

00:03:25.810 --> 00:03:31.690
Side note for any aspiring bank robbers: the
only time you should appear on TV is on Cops.

00:03:31.690 --> 00:03:33.260
DRUG TRAFFICKING PRODUCERS

00:03:33.260 --> 00:03:36.540
Even the people behind-the-scenes on Deadliest
Catch are magnets for trouble.

00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:40.810
Production manager Matthew Schneider was charged
in April 2010 for selling and using cocaine,

00:03:40.810 --> 00:03:42.750
according to The Associated Press.

00:03:42.750 --> 00:03:46.530
Schneider's illicit activities were discovered
after he allegedly sold about $300 worth of

00:03:46.530 --> 00:03:51.720
the stuff to an undercover officer—and used
some of it in front of the officer as well.

00:03:51.720 --> 00:03:52.720
Oops!

00:03:52.720 --> 00:03:56.090
He also revealed that some other show employees
were involved in a drug-trafficking affair,

00:03:56.090 --> 00:03:59.680
which resulted in the arrests of 18 people.

00:03:59.680 --> 00:04:01.430
HILLSTRAND BROTHERS ABANDON SHIP

00:04:01.430 --> 00:04:05.570
The best thing to happen to a breakout character
on a hit show is scoring a spin-off—unless

00:04:05.570 --> 00:04:06.980
they're the Hillstrand brothers.

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:12.160
In 2010, Discovery offered Jonathan and Andy
their own show, to be called Hillstranded.

00:04:12.160 --> 00:04:14.100
Discovery even started filming footage for
it.

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:17.760
However, when the time came to record voiceovers
and polish everything up, the brothers were

00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:20.190
nowhere to be found, according to E! Online.

00:04:20.190 --> 00:04:24.680
This didn't sit well with Discovery, who slapped
them with a $3 million lawsuit.

00:04:24.680 --> 00:04:28.980
The Hillstrands retaliated by leaving Deadliest
Catch altogether, taking fan-favorite Captain

00:04:28.980 --> 00:04:30.680
Sig Hansen with them.

00:04:30.680 --> 00:04:34.700
They all eventually made up, but the Hillstrands'
trouble didn't end there…

00:04:34.700 --> 00:04:35.700
FIREWORKS FOLLIES

00:04:35.700 --> 00:04:40.340
The Hillstrand brothers may need to hand over
some money to crew member David "Beaver" Zielinski,

00:04:40.340 --> 00:04:41.340
according to Seattle PI.

00:04:41.340 --> 00:04:45.910
In 2013, the Hillstrands wanted to celebrate
a Seattle Seahawks victory by shooting off

00:04:45.910 --> 00:04:50.060
some fireworks—because, yeah, shooting off
fireworks on a boat is a good idea.

00:04:50.060 --> 00:04:53.660
Under captain's orders, Zielinski lit off
a mortar like a foolishly obedient deckhand.

00:04:53.660 --> 00:04:58.200
The firework, which was made by the Hillstrands,
exploded while he held it, shattering the

00:04:58.200 --> 00:05:00.360
bones in his hand and forearm.

00:05:00.360 --> 00:05:03.720
Beaver filed his suit in 2015, seeking an
undisclosed amount.

00:05:03.720 --> 00:05:07.400
Looks like choppy waters ahead for the Hillstrands
after all...

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:09.300
ALASKA DISLIKES THE SHOW

00:05:09.300 --> 00:05:13.131
While viewers still love Deadliest Catch,
Alaska had its fill of the show, according

00:05:13.131 --> 00:05:14.580
to Alaska Dispatch News.

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:18.410
To summarize the complex issue, the boats
featured on the show are making things difficult

00:05:18.410 --> 00:05:20.820
for the rest of the northern crabbing fleet
to earn a living.

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:24.810
It seems that the Discovery Channel's funding
of fishing expeditions, in whole or part,

00:05:24.810 --> 00:05:27.530
has affected the crews not participating in
the show.

00:05:27.530 --> 00:05:29.520
That's made it difficult for them to keep
up.

00:05:29.520 --> 00:05:34.300
In some cases, those crews end up earning
minimum wage, and crabbing "is far too dangerous"

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:35.920
for such miniscule pay.

00:05:35.920 --> 00:05:39.420
On the other hand, it does afford Discovery
Channel the opportunity to create a show about

00:05:39.420 --> 00:05:41.960
former fisherman now living on skid row.

00:05:41.960 --> 00:05:44.080
BEHIND THE SCENES FAKERY?

00:05:44.080 --> 00:05:47.920
Like most reality shows, Deadliest Catch is
guilty of dressing up the events that happen

00:05:47.920 --> 00:05:48.920
in real life.

00:05:48.920 --> 00:05:51.760
In their case, producers made it appear as
though one of the ships was in danger of being

00:05:51.760 --> 00:05:56.360
sunk by huge waves during a storm, which is
an honest hazard of crab fishing.

00:05:56.360 --> 00:06:00.920
However, the episode in which this was dramatized
was filmed in September 2008, while the waves

00:06:00.920 --> 00:06:04.490
themselves were filmed a month later, according
to The Hollywood Reporter.

00:06:04.490 --> 00:06:07.680
Unsurprisingly, the Discovery Channel denies
any trickery.

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:08.680
Caught red-handed?

00:06:08.680 --> 00:06:10.110
Or perhaps red-clawed?

00:06:10.110 --> 00:06:11.410
Thanks for watching!

00:06:11.410 --> 00:06:14.510
Subscribe to our YouTube channel to see more
videos like the one you just saw.

00:06:14.510 --> 00:06:17.330
And leave us a comment to tell us what surprised
you the most about The Deadliest Catch crew...

